# NOTE: this is just a placehold and test script, people will rewrite it
# KLIMA GEM — the show, played AS Aurora.
# Ren hosts (a voice on the microphone, never rendered). You ARE Aurora: the
# only portrait on the stage, and every choice is her action. She throws two
# flat-topped gems, eight words each: the first names a modification, the
# second a body part. Whatever face lands front-most is the word the stage
# enforces. Three trials; every word helps somewhere and hinders somewhere,
# and each trial is decided by her actions plus the gems — no dice. Banter is
# seeded and throws are seeded physics, so the same night always replays.
# NOTE: this is 
using GameState
using ShowDirector

~ show_start
do begin_show()
I step into the light and the studio finds me\: a round stage under cold neon, a cloth of slow stars, and a sign that says KLIMA GEM. Below the apron the audience holds its glowsticks like candles. [#bg=none, #sprite=none:left, #sprite=none:right, #music=festival]
do enter_ren()
Ren: Good evening, good evening — every dimension currently tuned in! You are live at the Klima Gem stage, and I am Ren\: your host, your referee, and — by default, because nobody else applied — the funniest man in this reality.
Ren: New viewers, here is the entire rulebook. This show has one prop and no mercy. The gems.
Ren: Each gem is cut flat on top and worded on every slanted face — eight words apiece. My guest throws two of them, and whatever face lands front-most is LAW.
Ren: The first gem names a modification. The second names a body part. Modification meets body part... and reality, obligingly, agrees.
Ren: Then we play three trials on this stage. The gems set the situation before every trial — each word helps somewhere and hinders somewhere — and Aurora's actions decide the rest. No dice, no nets. The stage provides the obstacles. The crowd provides the noise.
Ren: And now — the moment the ratings wait for. From the Chrono Nexus itself, trembling politely at her own mark... my guest... AURORA!
do aurora_enters()
[#sfx=open]
Aurora: H-hello! Um. Aurora. Subsystem construct of the Chrono Nexus, and — apparently — tonight's contestant. That's me. I'm the contestant. (Why did I say that out loud.)
Aurora: I did read the contract. The one sentence I understood said the show is not responsible for gravity.
Ren: That sentence is the show, Aurora. Now — the crowd wants to know what kind of night this will be. How do we open?
- I take a breath and belt the hello. Big lights, big voice, finale before we begin.
	do add_trust(1)
	Ren: YES. That is the energy. Roll the intro like we stole it!
	The audience answers with a wall of noise, and the glowsticks blur into one bright wave.
- I wave small and steady. Let the gems speak first, dazzle them later.
	do add_bond("ren", 1)
	Ren: A soft opening. Very classy. Chaos is scheduled for later; it signed a form.
	Aurora: ...thank you. I'm fairly sure the gems can smell panic. Better they smell confidence first.
Ren: Aurora's hands on the gems. Crowd, hold your hearts. THROW!
=> round_intro

~ round_intro
do next_round()
if show_round == 1:
	Ren: Trial one of three\: {{challenge_name(show_round)}}. The floor is about to stop being a floor.
	Aurora: (The Crossing wants composure and confidence — my bond with Ren and my trust. Steady heart, steady feet.)
elif show_round == 2:
	Ren: Trial two of three\: {{challenge_name(show_round)}}. Precision round. The props have feelings and none of them are kind.
	Aurora: (Bell Barrage wants confidence and punch — my trust and my power. Aim like I mean it.)
else:
	Ren: The final trial\: {{challenge_name(show_round)}}. Everything from here on is memory and nerve.
	Aurora: My palms are sweating and I don't even have palms right now. Metaphorically sweating!
	Aurora: (The Echo Choir wants bond and memory — my bond with Ren and my insight. Listen, remember, sing back.)
do build_challenge(show_round)
if show_round == 1:
	A tear opens across the stage floor, deep violet and patient. Four flat stones float over it in a lazy diagonal, each one lit from below like a thought.
elif show_round == 2:
	A brass little cannon wheels in at stage left and aims itself at a rack of three golden bells, stage right. It polishes its aim. Nobody asked it to.
else:
	Four podiums rise in a gentle arc at the back of the stage, each topped with a glowing pad of a different hue. They hum in a chord that expects to be remembered.
=> gem_round

~ gem_round
do set_aurora_expression("serious")
Ren: Two gems. Eight words each. One body, about to be renegotiated. [#sfx=open]
Aurora: My throw. My hands. Here we go.
do throw_gem_round()
Ren: The stones land... and the words step OUT of them, glowing! Read them with me — first, the shapeshift!
Ren: {{show_mod}}!
[#sfx=confirm]
do set_aurora_expression("surprised")
Ren: And the body it lands on...
Ren: {{show_part}}!
[#sfx=confirm]
Ren: By decree of two rocks\: {{show_part}} x {{show_mod}}. The show accepts. Reality complies.
do apply_mods()
%3 The crowd loses its collective mind. Somewhere in the dark a horn section hits a note it will regret by morning.
%2 A ripple runs the length of the glowstick wave. Even the painted stars on the cloth seem to lean in.
do set_aurora_expression("surprised")
Aurora: I can FEEL it. That is... aggressively my {{show_part}} now.
if stack_word(show_mod) == "x2 — doubled":
	Ren: And that's {{show_mod}} TWICE on one guest! The shift compounds — double the effect, wherever it cuts.
	Aurora: Two of the same? My body is starting to take it personally.
elif stack_word(show_mod) != "":
	Ren: {{show_mod}} again — that's three or more! The body ADAPTS, folks\: from here on that shift only ever works in her favour.
	Aurora: Fine. FINE. If I'm going to be this much {{show_mod}}, I'm going to be good at it.
if show_part == "VOICE" and show_mod == "STICKY":
	Aurora: When I try to speak, words come out... attached to things. This is going to be a legal situation.
if show_part == "EYES" and show_mod == "GLOWING":
	Aurora: I can see the infrastructure of the stage. The scaffolding of reality has [b]EXPOSED BOLTS[/b], Ren.
if show_part == "HEART" and show_mod == "HEAVY":
	Aurora: My chest has a ballast now. Emotionally I remain very light. Physically the engineers disagree.
if show_outlook == "advantage":
	Ren: And read the board, folks — the odds just leaned HER way. Gems plus everything she's done tonight\: an advantage!
	%2 Aurora: The gems like me tonight. I have decided to be terrified by that in a productive way.
	%3 Aurora: Fortune favors the bold! And also, specifically, me!
elif show_outlook == "disadvantage":
	do set_aurora_expression("sad")
	Ren: Oh no. Oh no, no. Gems plus everything so far — the board calls it a disadvantage, and the board on this stage is never wrong.
	Aurora: The gems have chosen mischief and I respect the craft.
	Ren: There is a cheat code, though. One crowd cheer buys a re-throw of the modification gem. We are holding {{show_cheers}}.
	if show_cheers <= 0:
		Ren: ...which is to say, the jar is EMPTY. No cheers, no cheat code — play the hand!
	- I spend the cheer. The modification gem goes back into the air. [if show_cheers > 0 /]
		do swap_mod_gem()
		Ren: The producer weeps. The audience ROARS. New words — and the new pairing is... {{show_part}} x {{show_mod}}!
		%2 Aurora: A second chance! On live television! I will not waste it, probably!
		%3 Aurora: The gem came back DIFFERENT. They're individuals, Ren. I don't think we're supposed to know that.
	- I keep the bad hand. I play it with style.
		do add_bond("ren", 1)
		do set_aurora_expression("serious")
		Aurora: No swap. If I'm going to be ridiculous, I'll be ridiculous CONFIDENTLY.
		Ren: That is the bravest sentence ever spoken on this stage, and I once hosted a volcano wedding.
else:
	Ren: A fair draw! No favor, no curse — just nerve versus design.
	%2 Aurora: Balanced. Like a good gem. Like ME. Balanced!
	%3 Aurora: An honest roll! Do honest rolls get applause, or just quiet respect?
Ren: The stage is set, the words are worn. Tonight's odds for my guest\: {{outlook_word(show_round)}}. Roll them!
=> trial

~ trial
Ren: No do-overs, no nets, no refunds. Trial {{show_round}} — on my mark... begin!
Aurora: (Actions, not luck. What I've built tonight is what I've got.)
do run_challenge()
if last_success:
	do set_aurora_expression("happy")
	%2 Ren: CLEAR! Text the stars — she made it look rehearsed!
	%3 Ren: CLEAR! I felt that one in my resumé!
	A star peels off the pedestal, arcs across the stage, and lands with the others. Gold on gold.
	- I check my footing first. Technique deserves the note.
		do add_insight(1)
		Ren: Footwork, timing, angle of descent — text-book. I'd say lucky, but luck doesn't bend like that.
		Aurora: My {{show_part}} did the thing! The GOOD thing!
	- I bow to the crowd. They carried me over.
		do add_bond("ren", 1)
		Ren: Give it up for the audience — that roar had LIFT!
		Aurora: I heard every single one of you. Even the weird whistle. Especially the weird whistle.
else:
	do set_aurora_expression("sad")
	%2 Ren: ...a miss. The klaxon of shame stays silent, but only because it handed in its notice.
	%3 Ren: A miss! A beautiful, televised miss. The replays will be merciless and I will watch every one.
	Aurora: I was SO close. My {{show_part}} almost listened.
	- I let Ren talk me down. Properly, not for the cameras.
		do add_bond("ren", 2)
		do add_trust(1)
		Ren: Camera two, take a cookie break. Aurora — the gems set the situation, but you threw them exactly right.
		Aurora: ...you mean that. Your voice does the thing where it stops performing. Thank you.
	- I turn the flop into a bit. The show must bite.
		do add_power(1)
		Ren: LIVE television, people — we don't hide the falls, we INTERVIEW them! Aurora, describe the failure in one word!
		Aurora: ...sparkly.
		Ren: She said SPARKLY, folks! That's the spirit! That's the show!
if show_round < 3:
	Ren: Reset the floor. Tear the props down, count the stars — we have {{show_stars}} — and bring on the next trial!
	=> round_intro
Ren: And that's the show... well. That's the show on the scorecard. The scorecard doesn't know everything.
=> finale

~ finale
do set_aurora_expression("serious")
The stage stands empty again\: props struck, gems dimmed to embers on their pedestal. Only the sign and the slow stars keep working overtime.
if show_stars == 3:
	do set_aurora_expression("gorgeous")
	do finale_confetti()
	Ren: THREE STARS! A PERFECT SHOW! I have hosted one hundred and nine of these and I have seen this exactly never!
	Golden rain falls over the round stage, catching in my light like the whole sky decided to audition for me.
	Aurora: Three for three. My {{show_part}} is still modified, by the way. The modification stays until the credits. It's in the contract.
	Ren: Then stand there, exactly like that, being a {{show_part}} of {{show_mod}} — because that is the most Klima Gem image this stage has ever produced.
elif show_stars == 2:
	do set_aurora_expression("happy")
	Ren: TWO STARS out of three! A fine show! A strong show! The kind of show that gets a second season and a slightly bigger cannon!
	Aurora: Two stars and one honest miss. I can live in those numbers. I EARNED those numbers.
	Ren: The gem still says {{show_part}} x {{show_mod}} on its face, you know. It's grown on me. Like weather.
else:
	do set_aurora_expression("sad")
	Ren: One star, or none. A rough night at the Klima Gem. But hear me — nobody throws two gems like that and walks out a nobody.
	Aurora: The words were against me all night. But I threw them anyway. On camera. That has to count somewhere.
	Ren: It counts here. Trust me. I'm the host.
if show_stars >= 1 and can_read_mind("ren"):
	A quiet channel opens — the resonance the Nexus leaves between us, the one that lets me hear him when my bond with him runs deep enough.
	Aurora: (What he isn't saying into the microphone is that he watched every throw like it mattered. That's the prize I'm taking home.)
Ren: For my guest tonight — Aurora of the Chrono Nexus\: {{show_stars}} stars, {{rerolls_used}} mercies spent, and one stage that will remember her {{show_part}}.
do set_aurora_expression("happy")
Aurora: Same stage next season?
Ren: Same stage. New words. Maybe fewer cannon-related injuries.
Aurora: ...no promises about the cannon.
The lights take a last bow around the round stage, and the sign hums KLIMA GEM into the dark like a promise it intends to keep.
=> END
